aquila-radio-astronomy (0.2.23) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hydrogen line only: three parts of a scan are on the line and one on the
    reference, as in the narrowband search. It was half and half.
  * Settings: centre frequency, FFT size and raw IQ are greyed out while the
    narrowband search is off, since a hydrogen line scan does not use them. The log
    and the status show the frequency the receiver is tuned to.
  * Settings: the bandwidth list shows the sample rates the plugged in Airspy or
    HydraSDR has, and the default is one it has.
  * Airspy chosen with a HydraSDR plugged in now observes.
  * RTL-SDR: with two dongles plugged in, Settings and the first setup list them
    one by one (RTL-SDR #1, #2) so the one to use can be picked.
  * An observer no longer stays running after the app is killed or crashes.
  * hline --blocks ends with an error when no scan could be made.

 -- Ayushman Tripathi <ayushmantripathi7724@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:08:41 -0500

aquila-radio-astronomy (0.2.22) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 3D plot and day view: a peak is drawn as high as it was measured. A short peak
    was drawn lower, by an amount that changed from day to day.
  * RTL-SDR: the bias tee is off until it is turned on in Settings. An install that
    already has it on keeps it on.
  * RTL-SDR: with two dongles on one computer, the one to use can be named in the
    config file (advanced.device, a serial or an index).

 -- Ayushman Tripathi <ayushmantripathi7724@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:33:32 -0500

aquila-radio-astronomy (0.2.21) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Settings: OK with the receiver on Auto no longer clears the saved gain and
    sample rate.
  * Windows: Stop, or closing the window, while the node is starting now stops it.
    A receiver that sends no samples no longer holds the node.
  * Windows: closing the app no longer leaves an error in the Windows event log.
  * A table damaged by a power cut no longer stops the candidate list, the trimming
    of old rows or the lists in the app.
  * The candidate list is no longer worked out with the receiver the node is using.
  * The window keeps updating when the address of a far node is not a node.
  * RTL-SDR: the bias tee is switched off when it is set off. The test signal now
    works on RTL-SDR and HackRF.
  * Day view and 3D plot: no empty stripes at high sample rates or with scans far
    apart.
  * 3D plot: the numbers and labels at the side are no longer cut in a narrow
    window.
  * Smaller fixes in Settings, Quick setup, the Log tab and the sky map.

 -- Ayushman Tripathi <ayushmantripathi7724@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:48:09 -0500

